{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-x5rw-q4pp-hg5g","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-x5rw-q4pp-hg5g","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x5rw-q4pp-hg5g","summary":"devalue: stringifyAsync can cause an unhandled rejection despite a caught returned promise","description":"When serializing multiple promises, a later promise can reject before an earlier one settles. An internal rejected promise remains unhandled even if the caller catches the returned `stringifyAsync` promise. Under Node's default unhandled-rejection behavior this can terminate the process. Applications whose asynchronous failures/timing can be influenced by requests are potentially exposed.\n\nThis is essentially impossible to exploit, and is much more likely to surface as a developer-introduced bug.","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/devalue/security-advisories/GHSA-x5rw-q4pp-hg5g","source_code_location":"https://github.com/sveltejs/devalue","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-x5rw-q4pp-hg5g","type":"GHSA"}],"references":["https://github.com/sveltejs/devalue/security/advisories/GHSA-x5rw-q4pp-hg5g","https://github.com/sveltejs/devalue/commit/dae8153e9d7541b975cc4018138d6cebec6c1199","https://github.com/sveltejs/devalue/releases/tag/v5.9.3","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x5rw-q4pp-hg5g"],"published_at":"2026-10-01T15:15:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T15:15:15Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-10-01T15:15:13Z","nvd_published_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"devalue"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 5.8.0, <= 5.9.2","first_patched_version":"5.9.3","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":8.2}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-248","name":"Uncaught Exception"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-755","name":"Improper Handling of Exceptional Conditions"}],"cr